          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "7. Observe the activities in your house for a day. Identify the activities that involve evaporation. How does understanding the process of evaporation help us in our daily activities?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.255,
            0.213,
            0.785,
            0.234
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "8. How is water present in the solid state in nature?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.255,
            0.242,
            0.883,
            0.282
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "9. Reflect on the statement “Water is our responsibility before it is our right.” Share your thoughts."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.256,
            0.29,
            0.882,
            0.332
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "10. The seat of a two-wheeler parked on a sunny day has become very hot. How can you cool it down?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.389,
            0.369,
            0.639,
            0.394
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Learning further"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.257,
            0.426,
            0.883,
            0.483
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Wet one hand with water and leave the other dry. Blow air across both hands and feel the cooling effect. Find out the reasons for it."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.257,
            0.489,
            0.883,
            0.566
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Make a game to navigate through different states of water and water related concepts to reach the finish line. Challenge cards with questions related to water cycle, evaporation, condensation, etc., can be some game elements."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.257,
            0.571,
            0.883,
            0.611
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Discuss with your teacher and act out the stages of the water cycle through a role-playing activity in your school assembly."
            }
          ]
        },
